          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"40\") (name \"/NET0039\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"R43\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"R55\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"T3\") (pin \"3\") (pinfunction \"C\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"T8\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"G\") (pintype \"passive\")))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If the duplicate net name is interpreted as the same net, the Nutrient-B motor phase is shorted to the ATO-valve MOSFET gate. This would allow the motor output to drive or disturb the valve gate, load the motor phase with gate capacitance and pull-down/pull-up networks, and can cause incorrect valve actuation or damage to the driver/switch.",
      "confidence": 0.65
